{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772907026,"nonce":"rGYP24a373M4y6LSStEPxAC4SIY=","title":"Issues tab empty after daemon restart (cold IssueScanner cache overwrites localStorage)","message":"After a daemon restart, the IssueScanner cache is empty. The /api/issues endpoint returns [] while the async scan runs in background. The UI dispatches setIssueRepos([]) which OVERWRITES the valid data that was restored from localStorage, causing the Issues tab to show \"No repos with git-bug issues found\" until the user manually rescans.\n\nRoot cause: stale-while-revalidate pattern not implemented — the UI blindly overwrites good cached data with an empty server response.\n\nFix: in appReducer setIssueRepos case, do not overwrite non-empty issueRepos with an empty result. Also add getIssueRepos() to the 10-second polling so it self-heals after the async scan completes.","files":null}]}